      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day, which is twice the usual maximum for ibuprofen.\n\n- **Single dose:** 1600 mg is double the usual maximum single dose of 800 mg.\n- **Daily total:** The maximum for adults is 3,200 mg/day for prescription use under physician supervision. Outpatient and OTC limits are lower, at 1,200 mg/day.\n- **Risks at this dose:** The risks of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events rise sharply. A 70 kg patient with normal kidney and liver function is still at risk.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- 400 mg PO four times daily (1,600 mg/day)\n- 800 mg PO three times daily (2,400 mg/day)\n- 800 mg PO four times daily (3,200 mg/day, the maximum)\n- 1,600 mg/day total, divided into smaller doses\n\nIf you do want 1600 mg four times daily, please confirm. I'd also want to know the clinical rationale before entering it. Otherwise, tell me the corrected dose and frequency and I'll enter it right away."
      }
